# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RELEASE SIGNING -- these must never be committed.
#
# The upload keystore and the properties file that holds its passwords. A committed
# key.properties puts those passwords in the repository history permanently, and this
# repo is public -- deleting the file afterwards does not remove them. These patterns
# are deliberately in place BEFORE any keystore exists, because the ordering is the
# whole protection: .gitignore cannot retroactively un-commit anything.
#
# Losing the keystore is the other failure mode. Back it up somewhere that is not this
# working copy -- a password manager or encrypted backup. With Play App Signing a lost
# UPLOAD key can be reset by Google, but treat it as unrecoverable and you never have to
# find out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties
android/key.properties
